  "question": {
    "text": "In an oligopeptide named Alanylglycylphenyl alanyl isoleucine, the number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybridised carbons is&nbsp;_____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>An oligopeptide is a short-chain peptide. The given&nbsp;oligopeptide is a tripeptide.</p><p>The given Oligopeptide has the following structure</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/122eed9c-f3db-4d52-93bc-865e3fb48d48.png\" style=\"width: 530px; height: 120px;\" /></p><p>In&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridisation carbon can have one pi bond. The carbons marked with * are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;carbons</p><p>It has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> atoms.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
